pixel-ksu-root
==============

This project obtains temporary kernel read/write on a stock, locked-bootloader
Google Pixel via a userspace kernel exploit, then late-loads a KernelSU loadable
kernel module and hands control to the installed KernelSU manager. It works with
general KernelSU variants and is manager-agnostic.

It incorporates third-party work as noted below.


Vendored exploit (./exploit)
----------------------------

The exploit source under ./exploit implements CVE-2026-43499 ("GhostLock"), a
futex/rtmutex priority-inheritance stack use-after-free in kernel/locking/rtmutex.c.

Exploit and technique:
  NebuSec (Nebula Security), "IonStack Part II — GhostLock", in the CyberMeowfia
  repository. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Discovery credited
  to NebuSec's VEGA tooling; disclosed 2026-07-07.
  https://github.com/NebuSec/CyberMeowfia
  https://nebusec.ai/research/ionstack-part-2/
  https://nebusec.ai/buglist/CVE-2026-43499/

Pixel/aarch64 adaptation:
  The vendored tree under ./exploit adds android14-6.1 and android15-6.6 target
  offsets and a KernelSU late-load daemon on top of the NebuSec exploit. It
  carries no separate in-tree LICENSE file and inherits the NebuSec Apache-2.0
  terms above.

The vendored exploit retains its upstream Apache-2.0 license. A copy of the
Apache License, Version 2.0, is available at:
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

KASLR heap-pointer side channel:
  KernelSnitch — Lukas Maar et al., TU Graz (isec-tugraz), NDSS 2025.
  https://github.com/isec-tugraz/KernelSnitch
  https://lukasmaar.github.io/papers/ndss25-kernelsnitch.pdf


KernelSU LKM / ksud mechanism
-----------------------------

The late-load path builds on the KernelSU project's loadable-kernel-module and
ksud "late-load" mechanism: runtime symbol relocation against /proc/kallsyms,
the init_module(2) load, and in-kernel APK-signature manager authorization.
This project loads a prebuilt kernelsu.ko and drives ksud; it ships no KernelSU
source and does not modify the driver.
  KernelSU: https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU
